+| `held_sda_release.cpp` | Real `release_held_sda()` against a peripheral left inside a byte by a reset: every held position of the UnitNFC bytes and others, a receiver in its acknowledge slot, a peripheral that never lets go (exactly 10 pulses, then failure), SCL held low and an idle bus; at most 10 SCL pulses |
 | `detect_class_host.cpp`, `detect_session_host.cpp` | Detect-class matching and session verdict/preference/candidate/persistence rules |
 
 The fixtures record the complete semantic fields
diff --git a/test/board_detect/held_sda_release.cpp b/test/board_detect/held_sda_release.cpp
index fc6b9e8..607e305 100644
--- a/test/board_detect/held_sda_release.cpp
+++ b/test/board_detect/held_sda_release.cpp
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@ int main()
     assert(run({bits, 8, false, false}, &pulses));
     assert(pulses <= 10);
   }
+  // A peripheral that never lets go of SDA, not even for a STOP: the clocking is bounded.
+  assert(!run({std::vector<bool>(9, false), 0, false, false}, &pulses));
+  assert(pulses == 10);
   // SCL held low by someone else: give up instead of clocking.
   assert(!run({byte_bits(0x00), 0, true, true}, &pulses));
   assert(pulses == 0);
